          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_6449X3": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "How much room will I need (container sizes)?",
            "icon": "check_mark",
            "row_content": "<p><strong>1-gallon Jugs</strong><br/><strong>PLASTIC</strong> - 12\" h x 6\" w - with pump 17\" h<br/><strong>GLASS</strong> - 11\" h x 5.25\" w - with pump 16\" h<br/><br/><strong>5-gallon Eco-Jug</strong><br/><strong>VERTICAL</strong> - 14.5\" h x 10.5\" d x 10\" w - with economy pump 20\" h<br/><strong>VERTICAL</strong> - 14.5\" h x 10.5\" d x 10\" w - with premium pump 30\" h<br/><strong>HORIZONTAL </strong>- 14.5\" h x 10.5\" d x 10\" w - with spout 17\" d<br/><br/><strong>5-gallon Buckets</strong><br/><strong>BUCKET</strong> - 15\" h x 12\" d/w - with pump 21\" h<br/><br/><strong>30-gallon Drum</strong><br/><strong>Drum</strong> - 29\" h x 19\" d/w - with 30 g pump 38 to 48\" h (when extended)<br/><strong>Drum</strong> - 29\" h x 19\" d/w - with 55 g pump 44 to 54\" h (when extended)<br/><br/><strong>55-gallon Drum</strong><br/><strong>Drum</strong> - 35\" h x 24\" d/w - with 55 g pump 44 to 54\" h (when extended)</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "134fe9fd-e362-4888-8369-f0d7318c065c": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "How much laundry detergent should I use? Do you have an exact calculation?",
            "icon": "check_mark",
            "row_content": "<p>An exact calculation would only work under perfect conditions and every person's laundry set up is different.  We recommend starting with 1/2 to 1 oz of laundry detergent per load and adjust to your personal liking and efficiency. </p><p>The factors that affect dosage amounts are:</p><p><strong>Water type -</strong> </p><p>Hard water vs soft water</p><p>Well water vs city water</p><p>Mineral types found in the water</p><p>Hot water vs cold water</p><p><strong>Washing machine-</strong></p><p>Different machines work at different levels of efficiency. Also the amount of water added<br/>in a \"normal\" load will vary machine to machine. </p><p><strong>Soil level- </strong></p><p>The heavier the soil load on the clothes the more laundry detergent will be required to be effective. </p><p><strong>Machine load-</strong></p><p>The larger the load of garments in a machine the larger the laundry detergent load will be required. Especially true in older machines where the use is required to select the load size. Newer machines typically load sense and deliver the amount of water needed for the load of the garments inside.</p><p>So, all of this put together equals; as you use a particular laundry detergent the best way to determine the amount to use is to test and tune based on your<br/>particular sets of circumstances.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "025d74b6-bd36-41f8-9d1e-4d34f1d79240": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Is your pallet wrap recyclable?",
            "icon": "check_mark",
            "row_content": "<p>Yes, it is!!! The plastic wrap we use is denoted as a category 4 in the recycling programs. You should be able to drop it in the boxes at Walmart or participating grocery stores.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "5c7be51c-5ea4-405f-86a3-c9677a082c07": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Can your laundry detergent be used on cloth diapers or reusable menstrual pads?",
            "icon": "check_mark",
            "row_content": "<p>YES!!! We also recommend using our OxyBoost Stain Remover in conjunction with cleaning these items.  Pre-soaking the above items helps remove those tough stains as well.  If you want them bright white again, just hang them out to dry in the sun.  It is a natural bleaching agent. </p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
