    "16503934304b8b7578": {
      "type": "collapsible-content",
      "blocks": {
        "1650393430b8752ec4-0": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "What are Rustic Strength's no-no ingredients?",
            "icon": "check_mark",
            "row_content": "<p>Our products do not contain any of these ingredients and here is why.<br/><br/><strong>• parabens</strong> – xenoestorgens (agents that mimic estrogen) that has been linked to cancer<br/><strong>• fragrances with phthalates</strong>– some can be toxic (phthalates); perceived clean vs real clean because of the smell<br/><br/><strong>• phthalates</strong>– can damage liver, kidneys, lungs and reproductive system<br/><br/><strong>• SLS and SLES</strong>can irritate eyes, skin and lungs. Tested on animals and not environmentally friendly<br/><br/><strong>• dyes</strong> – skin irritant<br/><br/><strong>• brighteners-</strong> chemicals that remain on the clothes to absorb UV light (naphthotriazolystilbenes, benzoxazolyl, diaminostilbene, disulfonate)</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "1650393430b8752ec4-1": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Plastic, Glass, Boxes... why so many choices?",
            "icon": "check_mark",
            "row_content": "<p>It's all about keeping our core values of sustainability by recycling, reusing and upcycling<br/>materials. <br/>• The plastic bottles that we sell come from other manufacturer's surplus of supply (avoiding the landfill).<br/>• The glass jugs are made locally (supporting local business)<br/>• The boxes can be reused, recycled or upcycled for crafts and other projects.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "1650393430b8752ec4-2": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Why do you use deionized water?",
            "icon": "check_mark",
            "row_content": "<p>The deionization process removes mineral ions such as sodium, calcium, iron, copper, chloride, and sulfate to make the water as PURE as possible.  </p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "1650393430b8752ec4-3": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Are your products cruelty free, vegan and gluten free?",
            "icon": "check_mark",
            "row_content": "<p>YES!! All of the product line is gluten free, vegan and cruelty free. Unless otherwise marked (lotion bars are not vegan)</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "8200a33d-645a-4548-a865-eeca99fb703c": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "How do you help control waste in the environment?",
            "icon": "check_mark",
            "row_content": "<p>We offer a unique <a href=\"/pages/close-the-loop-program\" title=\"Close The Loop Program\">Close The Loop™ Program</a> that encourages the end user to send back containers to be sanitized, and reused.  When customers do this, they are refilling their existing containers vs throwing them away. </p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "c8186c1d-d292-41e2-bb73-8feda9123469": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "What makes you a zero-waste manufacturer? How are you making a difference in the war on waste and saving our planet?",
            "icon": "check_mark",
            "row_content": "<p>• We make a conscious effort to recycle, reuse and upcycle all of the materials that come into our facility.  We purchase bottles and caps from other businesses that don't want or can't use them anymore.  These bottles would typically end up in a landfill somewhere.</p><p><br/>• All of our label stock is reused as paper for tickets, notes, formulations and even packing material. If we have leftover label parts, they are used as<br/>tape. </p><p><br/>• Boxes that we receive supplies in are reused to ship our products. We also shred them as filler paper in our boxes for shipping purposes.</p><p><br/>• If containers come in that are slightly damaged or discolored, we sell them as seconds.</p><p><br/>• We share a building with another company.  This helps decrease land usage and increase power-sharing.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        }
      },
